E` clause. For example, the condition `(an.name IS NOT NULL AND (an.name LIKE \'%a%\' OR an.name LIKE \'A%\'))` can be transformed into `(an.name IS NOT NULL OR an.name LIKE \'A%\') AND (an.name LIKE \'%a%\')`. This transformation simplifies the `WHERE` clause and reduces the complexity of the query execution."""\n\nQuery Rewrite 5:\n"""The rule replaces IN with INTERSECT for querying intersecting datasets to potentially improve index usage and query speed. It also rewrites conditions using the OR operator into a series of UNION ALL operations to enhance code maintainability and performance. Additionally, it uses EXCEPT instead of NOT IN or anti-joins to minimize duplicate row processing and optimize resource use, effectively reducing execution time."""\n\nQuery Rewrite 6:\n"""The rule optimizes direct `IS NULL` queries on indexed columns by efficiently using the index. It also eliminates redundant `IS NULL` checks on columns defined as `NOT NULL` and simplifies the query logic."""\n\nQuery Rewrite 7:\n"""The rule simplifies constant expressions upfront by transforming `(a<b AND b=c) AND a=5` into `b>5 AND b=c AND a=5`. It also eliminates redundant or tautological conditions and converts nonconstant values in range conditions to constants, facilitating the use of indexes and improving query speed."""'}], 'model': 'llama3:8b', 'max_tokens': 1024, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.1}}
